# Scene Breakdown: The Spilled Coffee Mystery
**Project:** Test Live Logger  
**Brand:** Beyond3Baje  
**Total Estimated Runtime:** ~2:15 - 2:30 minutes

---

## Scene 1: The Catalyst
**Focus:** The Hook / The Paradox  
**Estimated Duration:** 0:00 - 0:20 (20s)

| Element | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Visuals** | Extreme macro shot of a dark coffee drop hitting a pool; slow-motion ripples. Flickering candlelight on stone. Aggressive quill scratching on parchment. Title Card: *THE SPILLED COFFEE MYSTERY*. |
| **Audio** | Resonant, echoed water drop. Deep, minimalist pulsing cello. Sharp, rhythmic scratching of a quill. |
| **Narration Key Points** | Not a revolution of swords, but of liquid. A catalyst that sharpened the human mind. |
| **Pacing** | Very slow, deliberate, high tension. |

---

## Scene 2: The Great Divergence
**Focus:** The Intellectual Shift (Tavern vs. Coffee House)  
**Estimated Duration:** 0:20 - 0:55 (35s)

| Element | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Visuals** | Split screen contrast: Chaotic, warm, blurred tavern vs. structured, dimly lit, focused coffee house. Close-up of rising steam from a cup. |
| **Audio** | Audio panning: Left (muffled shouting/clinking) vs. Right (quiet murmuring/page turning). Subtle steam hiss. |
| **Narration Key Points** | The tavern was the domain of intoxication (ale); the coffee house was the sanctuary of clarity. |
| **Pacing** | Transition from chaotic/fast to calm/observational. |

---

## Scene 3: The Penny Universities
**Focus:** The Democratization of Knowledge  
**Estimated Duration:** 0:55 - 1:25 (30s)

| Element | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Visuals** | Panning through 18th-century London sketches (ghost-like figures). Close-up of a weathered copper penny hitting a wooden table. |
| **Audio** | Light, scholarly orchestral track (pizzicato strings). A heavy, metallic *thud* for the coin. |
| **Narration Key Points** | The "Penny University." Social hierarchy suspended. The currency was ideas, not gold. |
| **Pacing** | Rhythmic, building momentum and curiosity. |

